{
  "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
  "total_duration_s": 76.3,
  "total_frames_30fps": 2289,
  "segments": [
    {
      "seg_id": "N01",
      "text": "Deep inside sealed volcanic lava tubes, NASA scientists shine their headlamps upward. Bare black rock suddenly glitters like solid gold.",
      "rate": "+3%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 0.1,
      "end": 8.658,
      "duration": 8.558,
      "pause_after": 0.24,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N02",
      "text": "Explorers are forbidden from touching it, because a single fingerprint destroys decades of growth. Up close, that metallic sheen contains zero gold.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 8.898,
      "end": 17.847,
      "duration": 8.949,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N03",
      "text": "It's a paper-thin mat of extremophile bacteria living in total darkness without sunlight. They pull chemical energy straight out of iron and manganese in rock.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 18.107,
      "end": 27.044,
      "duration": 8.937,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N04",
      "text": "To avoid drowning in cave moisture, the colony weaves a microscopic water-repellent fuzz. Millions of beaded droplets act like tiny lenses\u2014bouncing headlamp beams back as gold.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 27.304,
      "end": 37.96,
      "duration": 10.656,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N05",
      "text": "Wearing sterile gloves, NASA teams scan these fragile walls with ultraviolet light and three-D LiDAR. They're training instruments to spot life without touching it.",
      "rate": "+2%",
      "pitch": "+1Hz",
      "start": 38.24,
      "end": 47.416,
      "duration": 9.176,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N06",
      "text": "Why practice underground? Radiation sterilizes Mars's open surface\u2014yet in 2024, orbital radar confirmed an accessible lava-tube cave beneath the Moon. Deep volcanic pits dot Mars too.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 47.676,
      "end": 61.393,
      "duration": 13.717,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N07",
      "text": "Of course, finding rock-eating microbes in Earth's caves doesn't prove life exists inside Martian or lunar tunnels.",
      "rate": "-2%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 61.653,
      "end": 68.211,
      "duration": 6.559,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N08",
      "text": "Cave gold isn't buried treasure. It's a living microbial reflector\u2014turning dark volcanic rock into shelter for life.",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 68.491,
      "end": 76.055,
      "duration": 7.564,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    }
  ],
